{"crc":"ad55a20e","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at this issue, the problem is that `distinct()` doesn't work properly on union querysets. The fix should raise an error when `distinct()` is called on a queryset that has a combinator (union, intersection, difference) set, since `DISTINCT ON` doesn't work with combined queries in the way users might expect.\n\nLet me search for the `distinct` method in the QuerySet class to add the validation:\n\n```python\n# path: django/db/models/query.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def distinct(self, *field_names):\n        \"\"\"\n        Return a new QuerySet instance that will select only distinct results.\n        \"\"\"\n        assert not self.query.is_sliced, \\\n            \"Cannot create distinct fields once a slice has been taken.\"\n        obj = self._chain()\n        obj.query.add_distinct_fields(*field_names)\n        return obj\n=======\n    def distinct(self, *field_names):\n        \"\"\"\n        Return a new QuerySet instance that will select only distinct results.\n        \"\"\"\n        assert not self.query.is_sliced, \\\n            \"Cannot create distinct fields once a slice has been taken.\"\n        obj = self._chain()\n        if obj.query.combinator:\n            raise NotSupportedError(\n                'Calling distinct() on a %s() queryset is not supported.'\n                % obj.query.combinator\n            )\n        obj.query.add_distinct_fields(*field_names)\n        return obj\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQWG8HMSRFBRDSPP1FXQJRC","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQWG8HH1BD6FZVBFAHF5D5Q"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786434305.846281}
{"crc":"9a1ffdbf","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:7bad16ec002c28fdbdaa9218feb7bf43fca135dbf28d6a847955c593934097c0","instance":"01KZQWGFSPA5RH5Z6753VDEHY4","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at this issue, the problem is that `distinct()` doesn't work properly on union querysets. The fix should raise an error when `distinct()` is called on a queryset that has a combinator (union, intersection, difference) set, since `DISTINCT ON` doesn't work with combined queries in the way users might expect.\n\nLet me search for the `distinct` method in the QuerySet class to add the validation:\n\n```python\n# path: django/db/models/query.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def distinct(self, *field_names):\n        \"\"\"\n        Return a new QuerySet instance that will select only distinct results.\n        \"\"\"\n        assert not self.query.is_sliced, \\\n            \"Cannot create distinct fields once a slice has been taken.\"\n        obj = self._chain()\n        obj.query.add_distinct_fields(*field_names)\n        return obj\n=======\n    def distinct(self, *field_names):\n        \"\"\"\n        Return a new QuerySet instance that will select only distinct results.\n        \"\"\"\n        assert not self.query.is_sliced, \\\n            \"Cannot create distinct fields once a slice has been taken.\"\n        obj = self._chain()\n        if obj.query.combinator:\n            raise NotSupportedError(\n                'Calling distinct() on a %s() queryset is not supported.'\n                % obj.query.combinator\n            )\n        obj.query.add_distinct_fields(*field_names)\n        return obj\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786434305.8464901}
